# Read by `docker build -f python/examples/demo-catalog.DOCKERFILE .` (BuildKit takes the
# .dockerignore named after the Dockerfile). Keeps the image to what Bazel builds from: no local
# secrets, no host build output. Paths are relative to the build context, the repo root.
.git
.claude
**/.env
**/.env.local
**/temporal.toml
bazel-*
user.bazelrc
.venv
.venv-bazel
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/__pycache__
python/examples/code_mode_memory/memories
